# Backend and Persistence

The backend is the source of truth for shared group data.

## Conceptual entities

Expected core relationships:

```text
User
  │
  └── GroupMember ── Group
                       │
                       └── Expense
                              │
                              └── ExpenseSplit
```

Do not duplicate derived balances as authoritative data unless there is a demonstrated performance requirement.

Balances should be derivable from expenses.

## IDs

Use stable unique IDs.

Do not use display names as identifiers.

Do not expose sequential IDs as security mechanisms.

## Timestamps

Persist creation/update timestamps consistently.

Use server-generated timestamps where supported and appropriate.

## Currency

Persist currency explicitly.

MVP:

```text
ARS
```

Do not implement currency conversion.

A group should have a defined currency.

## Soft deletion

Do not introduce soft deletion automatically.

If audit/recovery requirements later justify it, design it deliberately.

## Mapping

Backend DTOs/models should be mapped into domain models.

Do not let database SDK types leak throughout the application.

## Derived data

Prefer calculating:

- totals,
- balances,
- settlement suggestions

from expenses rather than storing redundant values.

If derived values are cached later, define invalidation/recalculation rules explicitly.
